WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:05.890
SPEAKER 1: Once you have a
set of your APIs outfitted

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:08.530
with API proxies,
now is the time

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:10.490
to share them with
your developers

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.060
so that they can
start consuming them.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.760
In Apigee, we refer
to the process

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:19.510
of getting your APIs into
the hands of your developers

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:22.210
as publishing your APIs.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.110
Publication requires the
following three steps--

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:30.610
creating API products,
registering developers,

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.130
and registering apps.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.110
Here's how it works.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:39.430
In Apigee, an API product
is a set of API proxies

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:42.340
that you want to bundle
together to offer to your app

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:43.900
developers.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:47.590
Create different API products to
address different app developer

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:48.580
needs.

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:51.730
App developers are
your API's customers,

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:54.520
so treat creation
of an API product

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:59.160
as you would any other product
you'd offer to a customer.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.330
Next, to be able to give
app developers access

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:05.780
to your API products, you'll
need to register your app

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:07.080
developers.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:09.950
If you have a developer
portal, app developers

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:11.630
can register themselves.

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:13.730
If you don't have
a developer portal,

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:17.780
you can use the Apigee Edge
API to provide a registration

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.560
form for app developers, or
you can register them yourself

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.680
using the Apigee Edge UI.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.840
The final step in
enabling a developer

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.580
to access your API product is
to register a developer app.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.830
Again, if you have
a developer portal,

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:37.230
an app developer can
register her app herself.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.320
If you don't have
a developer portal,

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:43.580
you can use the Apigee Edge API
to provide an app registration

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:47.180
form for app developers,
or you can register the app

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:51.890
on your developer's behalf
using the Apigee Edge UI.

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:54.200
When registering her
app, the developer

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.160
selects the API products
that her app needs to access.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:01.070
Once registered, the
developer is given a consumer

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:06.350
key, also known as a public
key, API key, or app key.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:10.280
Each app has a single
key that provides access

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:14.640
to all API products
associated with the app.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.780
The app developer codes
her app to present the key

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.780
to be able to access
the API product.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.300
This is the simplest form
of app-based security

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.480
that you can
configure for an API.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.700
Another useful
feature of these keys

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:32.420
is that you can revoke a key to
prevent an app from accessing

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:37.100
one or all of the API products
with which it is associated.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.190
And there you have it--
products, developers,

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:43.940
and developer apps and their
keys working in conjunction

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:47.090
to provide targeted
access to your APIs

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:49.250
to your app developers.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:53.570
To learn more about Apigee,
products, developers,

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:57.940
and developer apps, please
see the links provided.

